===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|ore|id=oar|t=oar}}, from {{inh|en|ang|ār}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*airu}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*airō||oar}}. Cognate with {{cog|non|ár}}.

===Pronunciation===
* In [[British]] & some other [[non-rhotic]] accents:
** {{a|RP}} {{IPA|en|/ɔː/}}
** {{a|nonrhotic|horse-hoarse}} {{IPA|en|/oə/}}
** {{homophones|en|aw|awe}} {{qualifier|in [[non-rhotic]] accents with the {{w|horse–hoarse merger}}}}
* In [[US]] & some other [[rhotic]] accents:
** {{a|GenAm}} {{enPR|ôr}}, {{IPA|en|/ɔɹ/}}
** {{audio|en|en-us-oar.ogg|Audio (US)}}
** {{a|rhotic|horse-hoarse}} {{enPR|ōr}}, {{IPA|en|/o(ː)ɹ/}}
** {{homophones|en|ore|o'er}}; {{l|en|or}} {{qualifier|in accents with the {{w|horse-hoarse merger}}}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɔː(ɹ)|s=1}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A type of [[lever]] used to [[propel]] a boat, having a flat [[blade]] at one end and a handle at the other, and pivoted in a [[rowlock]] atop the [[gunwale]], whereby a [[rower]] seated in the boat and pulling the handle can pass the blade through the water by repeated [[strokes]] against the water's [[resistance]], thus moving the boat.
#: {{syn|en|paddle}}
#* {{quote-song|1=en|year=19 October 1979|author=[[w:Madness (band)|Madness]]|title=[[w:Night Boat to Cairo|Night Boat to Cairo]]|lyricist=[[w:Suggs|Suggs]]|url=https://lyricstranslate.com/en/madness-night-boat-cairo-lyrics.html|album=|text=''The '''oar''' snaps in his hand<br/>Before he reaches dry land<br/>But the sound doesn't deafen his smile<br/>Just pokes at wet sand<br/>With an '''oar''' in his hand<br/>Floats off down the river Nile<br/>Floats off down the river Nile...''}}
# An [[oarsman]]; a [[rower]].
#: {{ux|en|He is a good '''oar'''.}}
# {{lb|en|zoology}} An oar-like [[swim]]ming [[organ]] of various [[invertebrate]]s.

